  "id": "Compound::DB00130 - Gene::2162",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset strongly suggests a mechanistic link between L-glutamine and F13a1. L-glutamine binds to Tgm6, Tgm4, and Tgm7, all of which participate in the Gamma-glutamyltransferase Activity pathway. This pathway is ultimately involved in the participation of F13a1, indicating a conserved biological process across these interactions. The high scores in all three paths (0.6553) suggest a robust and consistent relationship, likely due to the shared involvement of Gamma-glutamyltransferase Activity in the regulation of F13a1. The mechanism appears to involve L-glutamine modulating the activity of gamma-glutamyltransferase, which in turn affects F13a1. This pathway is likely critical for cellular processes involving protein modification and function, and the observed interactions imply that L-glutamine may influence F13a1 through a common intermediate. The evidence supports a direct, mechanistic relationship, though the exact role of each interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
